        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp",
        "Qi-Kun Xue"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Topological insulators and quantized edge transport exposed a new organizing principle for electronic matter, with lasting effects on condensed matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane's prediction and experimental realizations represented here by Molenkamp and Xue connect theory to observation, though the discovery involved other important contributors.",
        "maturity": "The phases and transport phenomena are well established, while many proposed applications remain research goals.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The long-term practical impact of topological devices is less settled than the scientific importance of the discoveries."
        ]
      }
    },
